    "id": "/",
    "text": "",
    "title": "MYCC",
    "summary": "## MYCC (Mindmap Knowledge System)\n\n`MYCC.md` is the project's self-description (guidance for Claude Code: terminology, architecture, loop, tools/skills). The **mindmap** compiles it into an LLM-enriched knowledge tree that is the agent's primary memory; the agent navigates it with the `recall` tool instead of loading MYCC.md wholesale.\n\n### Data model (`src/mindmap/types.ts`)\n`Node` = `id` (slash path from `/`), `text`, `title`, `summary`, `level`, `children`, `links` (`node|file|url|term`), plus **in-memory-only** flags `is_mycc` / `is_patch` (never serialized). Plus `Mindmap`, `ANCEContext`, `MindmapPatchAction`.\n\n### Two on-disk lines, merged in memory only (`src/loop/mindmap-loader.ts`)\n1. `.mycc/mindmap.json` — compiled isomorph of MYCC.md (`load.ts` sets `is_mycc=true`, `is_patch=false`).\n2. `.mycc/mindmap-patch.jsonl` — append-only `add`/`update`/`delete` log, **hash-gated** on `mindmap_hash`; replayed via `applyPatchAction`. `recall` marks children `[M]`/`[P]` and hoists all `term` links as **Key Terms** at `/`.\n\n### Compilation (`compile.ts`, `explorer-agent.ts`)\nHeading parse (code-block aware) → per-node Explorer Agent (≤25 rounds, tool set incl. `mark_term`, context compaction) → bottom-up **A-N-C-E** summarization (semaphore max 3) → `.new` → `.bak` atomic rotation → `wx` lock resumption (4h freshness) → patch rebuild.\n\n### Patch rebuild (`patch-jsonl.ts`)\n`validatePatchAction` rejects orphan-creating actions at both append and write. `rebuildPatches` BFS-walks the merged tree vs `basePaths`: `add` for patch-added nodes, `update` for `is_mycc && is_patch`, and **`add` for MYCC.md-deleted nodes** (content preserved).\n\n### Interfaces\n`src/slashes/mindmap.ts` (`compile [--force]`, `get`, `patch`, `validate`, `rebuild-patches`); `patch.ts` cascades summary regeneration; `diff-mindmap.ts` deprecated. Process isolation: lead `.mycc/mindmap.json`, teammates `.mycc/mindmap-{name}.json` — mindmap is *not* IPC (use wiki/mail/issues).\n\nDocs: `docs/mindmap/mindmap-design.md`, `mindmap-redesign.md`, `mindmap-usage.md`.",
    "level": 0,
