        "id": "/mycc.md",
        "text": "This file provides guidance for Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.",
        "title": "MYCC.md",
        "summary": "MYCC.md is the top-level guidance document for Claude Code in this repo — \"mycc\" (`@pkubangbang/mycc`, v0.11.8, pnpm-based), a Node.js coding agent using Ollama (default) or DeepSeek for inference (embeddings always Ollama), with AgentContext as the central state container.\n\nIt has eight parts. **Project Overview/Setup** — install plus Windows/PowerShell specifics (bash tool runs PowerShell, `psmux` replaces tmux, forward-slash paths, `/fork` via `-EncodedCommand`). **Terminology** disambiguates jargon: tools/skills/hooks/routine, built-in/project/user layers, session/turn/chat, populator vs system prompt, backlog/livelog/TP constraint, PROMPT vs prompt, autofly/streak, whisper/letter box, bang command, brief. **Architecture** documents AgentContext (Parent/Child), Triologue (facade over store/pending-tools/compact/wrap-up/brief/recap/truncate), AgentIO, IPC/IOC, Loader, the six-state machine, Sequence, Confusion Index, skill suggestion scoring, mindmap (patches + compile), wiki/LanceDB, auto-claim, health-check, hookish skills with jsep-validated lazy compilation, and the intent-based Grant system. **Modes & Team** covers normal/plan, lead/teammates, remote peer mail, todos/issues + preventStop guard, sealed sessions, slash commands, tool scopes. **WebUI Features** covers ServeHub, steering, file upload, neglection/ESC wrap-up, crossroad, `@teammate` routing and accordion UI. **Development** details testing (vitest, tmux), lint/typecheck, debug flags, Docker, built-in skills, scripts interop, Windows daemon wrapper. **Pitfalls** (DeepSeek gaps, agentIO in children, Loop Notation) and **Design Rationale & History** close the doc.",
        "level": 1,
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "/mycc.md/project-overview",
            "text": "This project builds a tool called \"mycc\" -- A node.js coding agent implementation using Ollama (default) or DeepSeek API for LLM inference. The architecture follows a modular design with AgentContext as the central state container. Two API providers are supported: Ollama (full features including web_search, screen, read_picture) and DeepSeek (cloud-based, no web_fetch tool — but web_search via the server-side Responses API and screen/read_picture via the deepseek-flash vision model are supported; prompt caching). Embedding for wiki/RAG always uses Ollama regardless of provider.",
            "title": "Project Overview",
            "summary": "## Project Overview\n\n**mycc** (package `@pkubangbang/mycc`, v0.11.8, described as \"Node.js agent implementations using Ollama — harness engineering for AI agents\") is a Node.js CLI coding agent that runs LLM inference through **Ollama** (default) or the **DeepSeek** cloud API. Architecture is modular, with **AgentContext** as the central state container (`src/types.ts`): `core`, `todo`, `mail`, `skill`, `issue`, `bg`, `team`, `wiki`, implemented as `ParentContext` (lead, direct access) and `ChildContext` (teammates, IPC wrappers).\n\n**Provider selection** is centralized: `getApiProvider()` in `src/config.ts` returns `'deepseek'` only when `API_PROVIDER=deepseek`, else `'ollama'`. `src/engine/chat-provider.ts` is a single facade that statically imports both `ollama.ts` and `deepseek.ts` and re-exports the active provider's `retryChat`, `retryMultipleChoice`, `webSearch`, `webFetch`, `imgDescribe`, `structuredChat`, `healthCheck` — plus the cache-preserving `forkChat`.\n\n**Capability matrix**\n- **Ollama (default)** — full features: streaming chat, `web_search`, `web_fetch`, vision (`screen`/`read_picture`) via `OLLAMA_VISION_MODEL` (no default; must be set). Default model `glm-5:cloud`.\n- **DeepSeek** (default model `deepseek-v4-pro`) — raw `fetch()` SSE against `POST /chat/completions`; `thinking` → `reasoning_content`, tool-call args serialized as JSON strings; thinking mode (`reasoning_effort: 'high'`, `max_tokens: 65536`) and **prompt caching**.\n  - `webFetch` **throws** `\"webFetch not supported by DeepSeek provider\"` — no `web_fetch` tool.\n  - `webSearch` works via `POST /responses` with `tools:[{type:'web_search'}]`; server-side, returning only the synthesized answer plus search/open_page summaries.\n  - `imgDescribe` works via base64 `image_url` blocks in a `user` message using `DEEPSEEK_VISION_MODEL` (default **`deepseek-flash`**); vision on by default, only `=none` disables.\n- **Embedding/RAG always uses Ollama** regardless of chat provider: `src/engine/rag-provider.ts` picks nomic vs embeddinggemma from `OLLAMA_EMBEDDING_MODEL` (default `nomic-embed-text`) and exports `getEmbedding`, `EMBEDDING_DIM`, `NAMESPACE`.\n\n**Config**: env layering user `~/.mycc-store/.env` → project `./.mycc/.env` → system env → CLI flags (highest). Key files: `src/config.ts`, `src/engine/chat-provider.ts`, `src/engine/ollama.ts`, `src/engine/deepseek.ts`, `src/engine/rag-provider.ts`, `src/types.ts`; `MYCC.md` is the canonical reference.",
