          {
            "id": "/mycc.md/architecture-core-concepts",
            "text": "**AgentContext** — the modular state container and central interface through which tools interact with the system. Modules: `core` (work dir, logging, user questions), `todo`, `mail` (async inter-agent mailbox), `team`, `issue`, `skill`, `bg`, `wt` (git worktree), `wiki`. Two implementations: `ParentContext` (main, direct access) and `ChildContext` (child, IPC wrappers).\n\n**Triologue** — the conversation state manager: tracks message history, manages `microCompact()`/`autoCompact()` for token management, tracks the `Sequence` for hookish skill conditions, supports hint round generation for confusion recovery. Since the 2026-08 layered refactor, `src/loop/triologue.ts` is a thin **facade** over sibling modules in `src/loop/triologue/`: `store.ts` (MessageStore — message array, token accounting, project-context populators, defensive hole filtering), `pending-tools.ts` (PendingToolLedger — pending tool-call resolution + alignment validation), `compact.ts` (transcript save, summary/focus prompts, `runAutoCompact` via a `CompactDeps` adapter), `wrap-up.ts` (WrapUpManager — wrapUpMark lifecycle), `brief.ts` (brief call parsing/isolation), `recap-note.ts` (brief result rendering), `truncate.ts` (shared truncate-and-recount), and `types.ts` (shared types incl. `TriologueInternals` — the narrow interface tp-fix.ts consumes instead of the full class; public API shrank by deleting dead `getMessagesFrom` and moving the five `_`-prefixed internals behind `TriologueInternals`).\n\n**AgentIO Singleton** (`src/loop/agent-io.ts`) — manages I/O state: the LineEditor (prompt input), ESC/neglected mode, process type detection. Key: `isMainProcess()` (true in lead, false in child/teammate), `isNeglectedMode()`/`setNeglectedMode(value)`, `onNeglected(callback)`, `ask(prompt)` (main-only), `exec(cmd)` (main-only), `execEditor(args)`. Bang mode: typing `!` at prompt start switches to `run cmd ! ` (`BANG_PROMPT`). **Child processes cannot use `ask()`/`exec()` — they throw.** Use `ctx.core.question()` (IPC) for user questions and `ctx.core.brief()` for logging.\n\n**IPC and IOC** — IPC enables main↔child communication via Node.js `child_process.fork()` and message passing. IOC: `TeamManager` acts as a dispatcher — modules register handlers for specific message types (Open-Closed Principle). Key: `IpcRegistry` (dispatcher), `sendRequest`/`sendNotification` (primitives), Request-Response pattern for operations requiring results.\n\n**Loader** — unified loading of tools and skills with hot-reload for dynamic content. Priority (highest wins): (1) built-in (`src/tools/`, `skills/`), (2) project (`.mycc/tools/`, `.mycc/skills/`), (3) user (`~/.mycc-store/`). Methods: `loadAll()`, `watchDirectories()` (hot-reload), `getToolsForScope(scope)`.\n\n**State Machine** — the agent loop uses explicit states instead of a single `while(true)`: **prompt** (get user input, handle slash/bang/exit), **collect** (pre-LLM pipeline: questions, mail, hint round, todo nudge), **llm** (build system prompt, call LLM with retry), **hook** (augment tool calls, evaluate hook conditions), **tool** (execute tool calls sequentially), **stop** (handle no-tool-call case, await teammates).\n\n**Sequence** — a wrapper around Triologue providing query methods for hookish skill conditions to inspect conversation history (`turn.lastIndex('edit_file')`, `session.count('bash')`, `turn.hadError('git_commit')`).\n\n**Confusion Index** — a metric quantifying how \"stuck\" an agent is, triggering hint rounds. Scoring: `+1` per assistant response, `+0` for exploration tools, `-1` for action tools, `+2` for tool errors, `+1` for repetition. When score >= threshold (default 10): main triggers hint round (LLM self-analysis); child sends mail to lead requesting guidance.\n\n**Skill Suggestion (proactive discovery, COLLECT step 6)** — after each turn the COLLECT state runs `skillSuggester.suggestSkill` (`src/loop/states/collect-skill.ts`, invoked from `collect.ts` step 6), a proactive skill-discovery pass that surfaces relevant skills the agent has NOT yet loaded. It composes a **composite text** from three sources: **brief** = `turn.lastBriefMessage` (the agent's self-reported focus, set in TOOL), **query** = the freshest steering note or `turn.lastUserQuery` (the **trigger source** — extraction runs ONLY when query changes), **hint** = `turn.lastHintFocus` (the hint round's `focus_on`, captured in step 3). The composite is sent to the SHARED LLM extractor (`extractKeywords` in `src/loop/keyword-extractor.ts`, the same primitive used by the on-demand `skill_search` tool, so discovery and search rank identically), which returns **significance-ordered** English keywords (most discriminative first, max 5 relevant) plus a free-form semantic query. Skills are then **scored** — no longer filtered by the old `min(Y-1,(X/W)*Y)` baseline gate. **Scoring contract** (shared byte-for-byte with `skill_search`): (1) **Positional points** — for each significance-ordered keyword `kw[i]` (i < 5), every skill owning `kw[i]` as an exact case-insensitive token earns `[10, 7, 5, 3, 2][i]` points (Motor-racing style); `points > 0` is a HARD precondition, so a pure-semantic skill can never surface (0 × anything = 0). (2) **Semantic boost** — `boost = 1 + (sim − getSkillMatchThreshold())` when `sim > threshold` (neutral 1.0 at the 0.5 threshold; 0.7 → 1.2, 0.9 → 1.4); a keyword-matched skill that misses the semantic window (or a failed wiki call) keeps `boost = 1.0` — it is **never excluded** on semantic grounds (soft boost, not intersection). (3) **score = points × boost**; keep `score > 10` STRICT; sort desc; take the **top 3**. Because points ≥ 12 passes unconditionally and points ≤ 5 never can, the gate lets keyword-strong matches stand alone while a 7–10 point match must ride a genuine semantic hit. The single semantic `ctx.wiki.get` call uses a **flat `topK = 50`** (NOT derived from `listSkills().length` — the `skills` wiki domain is SHARED ACROSS PROJECTS and accumulates other projects' rows, so the loaded-skill count is not an upper bound); a saturated window (`results.length === topK`) logs a warning. Ranked skills are partitioned by `getSkillTriologueStatus` (a private method on `SkillSuggester`) into three classes — **new** (never mentioned in the triologue), **suggested** (appeared in a prior `[HINT]` note or `skill_search` result), **loaded** (already `skill_load`-ed this session) — and a single `[HINT]` note is injected via `triologue.note('HINT', ...)` listing each class with a `skill_load(name=\"<exact_name>\")` call hint. **Throttling:** a 3-pass cooldown suppresses re-triggering from consecutive user messages; a `failed` extraction (ESC abort / transient error) does NOT consume the opportunity (query stays eligible for retry), while `success`/`skipped` (trivial greeting) mark query as seen; an empty `freeformQuery` on a `success` outcome **fails fast** via `clearThrottle()` so the next pass re-attempts extraction. **Discipline:** the note is a *silent nudge* — the agent either loads a genuinely helpful skill or stays silent and continues; it must NOT write a prose reply narrating its decision (that clutters the conversation and re-triggers the same nudge). (Historically a separate `--debug-suggest` flag logged a standalone SUGGEST background task; that task was folded into this in-loop `suggestSkill` pass and the flag is now obsolete — removed from `help.ts`/`README.md`. The keyword extractor and skill-dedup logic were previously standalone modules `src/loop/keyword-extractor.ts` and `src/utils/skill-dedup.ts`; the extractor is now the SHARED module consumed by both `collect-skill.ts` and `skill_search.ts`, and the dedup logic is a private method on `SkillSuggester`.)\n\n**mindmap** — a tree-structured knowledge system compiling markdown files (like `MYCC.md`) into a navigable JSON structure. Each node has an ID (slash-separated path), text, title, summary (LLM-generated), level, children, links. The agent queries nodes via `get_node`/`recall` for efficient context retrieval. Compilation is one-way: `MYCC.md --> [compile_mindmap] --> mindmap.json`. Each agent has an independent mindmap instance (process isolation). **Patch line**: agent-discovered knowledge is recorded as append-only patches in `.mycc/mindmap-patch.jsonl` (add/update/delete), replayed into the in-memory tree at load time. `/mindmap compile` rebuilds patches (BFS dedup/stale-removal) and **preserves MYCC.md-deleted nodes as `add` patches** so trimmed content survives as patch-added knowledge. See `docs/mindmap/mindmap-design.md` and `docs/mindmap/mindmap-redesign.md`.\n\n**wiki, vector store** — a persistent knowledge base using LanceDB for vector similarity search, with WAL (Write-Ahead Log) files for audit and rebuild. Each document has hash, domain, title, content, references, embedding vector. Components (`src/context/parent/wiki.ts`): `wiki.get/put/rebuild/listDomains`. Tools: `wiki_get`, `wiki_put`, `wiki_prepare`. Config: embedding model `nomic-embed-text` (`OLLAMA_EMBEDDING_MODEL`), duplicate threshold 0.95, content limits 50-1000 chars. WAL stored in `~/.mycc-store/wiki/logs/YYYY-MM-DD.wal`; rebuild via `/wiki rebuild`.\n\n**Auto-Claim** — idle child processes automatically claim unassigned issues. When a child enters IDLE state (no tool calls), it polls for new mail and scans issues for `pending` + no owner + no blockers, then atomically claims the first match.\n\n**health-check** — runs at startup to validate Ollama connectivity and model availability: (1) server reachable, (2) model exists and can process requests, (3) `TOKEN_THRESHOLD` ≤ 80% of model's context length. Implementation `src/setup/ollama-health-check.ts` (`checkHealth` → `HealthCheckResult`). CLI flag `--skip-healthcheck` bypasses; on failure, prompts retry or exit.",
            "title": "Architecture & Core Concepts",
            "summary": "Re-verified against source; the section is accurate with a few precise corrections.\n\n**AgentContext** (`src/types.ts`) composes eight modules: `core`, `todo`, `mail`, `skill`, `issue`, `bg`, `team`, `wiki` (there is no separate `wt`/`skill` split beyond these). `CoreModule` exposes `getWorkDir`, `brief`, `verbose`, `question`, `get/increase/resetConfusionIndex`, `escAware`, `requestGrant`.\n\n**Triologue** (`src/loop/triologue.ts`) is a facade over `triologue/`: `store.ts`, `pending-tools.ts`, `compact.ts`, `wrap-up.ts`, `brief.ts`, `recap-note.ts`, `truncate.ts`, `transcript.ts`, `tp-fix.ts`, `types.ts`. Teammates use the leaner `TriologueLite`.\n\n**AgentIO** (`src/loop/agent-io.ts`): `isMainProcessFlag`, `setNeglectedMode`, `onNeglected`; `ask()` throws in children. `BANG_PROMPT` lives in `src/utils/line-editor.ts`.\n\n**IOC/IPC**: `IpcRegistry` (`src/context/ipc-registry.ts`) dispatches; `sendRequest`/`sendNotification` in `child/ipc-helpers.ts`.\n\n**States** (`state-machine.ts`): PROMPT/SLASH/COLLECT/LLM/HOOK/TOOL/STOP/AWAIT + `MachineEnv`/`TurnVars`/`ChatData`.\n\n**Confusion**: `brief` delta `8−confidence`, +2 errors, −1 non-duplicate action, embedding-similarity delta; threshold 10 (`teammate-worker.ts`).\n\n**Skill suggestion**: `collect.ts` step 6 → `skill-matcher.ts#scoreSkills` (weights [10,7,5,3,2], floor 10 strict, top 3, semantic topK 50, scope-aware qualified-title boost).\n\n**Loader**: user→project→built-in (built-in wins). **Wiki**: LanceDB, 0.95 dup threshold, content 10–1000 *tokens* (not chars). **Health check** moved to `src/engine/health-check.ts` (`HealthCheckResult`, `probeModel`, `probeEmbeddingModel`) with per-provider `healthCheck()` in `ollama.ts`/`deepseek.ts`.",
            "level": 2,
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "/mycc.md/architecture-core-concepts/hookish-skills",
                "text": "Skills that actively trigger based on patterns in the conversation sequence (vs. passive skills loaded on explicit request). Defined with a `when:` field in YAML frontmatter. Condition language queries conversation history using two scope prefixes: `turn.*` (current turn, since last user query) and `session.*` (entire livelog, since session start or last compact). Functions: `turn.count(tool?)`, `turn.lastIndex(tool)`, `turn.countResult(tool, pattern, maxChars?)`, `turn.hadError(tool?)`, `session.count(tool?)`, `session.lastIndex(tool)`, `session.countResult(tool, pattern, maxChars?)`, `session.hadError(tool?)`, plus global `isPlanMode()`. Tool spec (three-class): plain tool (`\"toolName\"`), skill_load (`\"skill_load#skillName\"`), bash (`\"bash#commandPrefix\"` — clause-split by `;`/`&&`/`||`, then prefix match). Call context: `call.metadata.*` (filePath, newLoc, existingLoc, isDestructive), `call.args.*` (raw tool args). Actions: `inject_before`, `inject_after`, `block`, `replace`, `message`, `compact`.\n\n**Condition Compiler Principles** — translates natural-language `when` into structured `{ trigger, condition, action }` via a safety-first pipeline: (1) **Lazy Compilation** — conditions are NOT compiled eagerly; a skill with `when` is \"pending\" until `skill_compile` is invoked (pending hooks are injected into LLM context at startup). (2) **LLM Translation with Structured Output** — `when` is sent to the LLM with all tools and a JSON schema enforcing the output shape. (3) **Expression Safety via jsep AST** — conditions are parsed with jsep and walked recursively (NOT `eval`/`new Function`); only `turn`/`session`/`call` root identifiers, only known `turn.*`/`session.*` functions, no dangerous identifiers, only safe string/array methods on results. (4) **Retry with Error Feedback** — up to 3 retries. (5) **Smoke Test** — evaluate against an empty mock sequence before persisting. (6) **Atomic Persistence** — temp file + rename, with backup. (7) **Source File Tracking & Orphan Cleanup** — `sourceFile` as `\"{layer}:{path}\"`; orphans auto-removed. (8) **Version History** — every compilation creates a new version in the `history` array (full audit trail). Key files: `src/hook/conditions.ts`, `src/hook/condition-validator.ts`, `src/hook/evaluator.ts`, `src/tools/skill_compile.ts`.",
                "title": "Hookish Skills",
                "summary": "Hookish skills are skills whose YAML frontmatter carries a natural-language `when:` that compiles into a `{ trigger, condition, action }` hook evaluated against conversation history (vs. passive skills loaded on request). Conditions query `turn.*` (events since last turn boundary, cleared at STOP→PROMPT, survives compact) and `session.*` (whole livelog, cleared by `compactReset()`) via `count/lastIndex/countResult/hadError`, plus globals `isPlanMode()` and `totalTurns()` (both function-only — a bare identifier is rejected). Tool specs are three-class: `\"tool\"`, `\"skill_load#name\"`, `\"bash#prefix\"` (clause-split by `;`/`&&`/`||`, then prefix). Call context exposes `call.metadata.*` and `call.args.*`. Actions: `inject_before/inject_after/block/replace/message/compact`, ordered by HOOK_PRIORITY (compact/block → replace → inject → message) with per-chat dedup for injections and per-turn dedup for stop+block/replace.\n\nKey files: `src/hook/conditions.ts` (ConditionRegistry: lazy/pending compilation via `syncPending`, LLM structured-output translation with `CONDITION_SCHEMA`, MAX_COMPILE_RETRIES=3 with error feedback, trigger whitelist, atomic temp+rename persistence with `.backup`/rollback, orphan cleanup via `{layer}:{path}` `sourceFile`, `history` versioning, runtime `erroredConditions`), `src/hook/condition-validator.ts` (jsep AST walk, `ALLOWED_ROOTS`, `KNOWN_SCOPED_FUNCTIONS`, `DANGEROUS_IDENTIFIERS`, `smokeTestExpression` against `MockSequence`, `compileCondition()`), `src/hook/evaluator.ts` (no eval/new Function), `src/hook/sequence.ts`, `src/hook/hook-executor.ts`, `src/hook/hook-preprocessor.ts`, `src/tools/skill_compile.ts` (delegates to `ctx.skill.compileCondition`), `src/context/shared/loader.ts` (lead in-memory compile vs. child disk + `condition_replace` IPC), `src/loop/hook-bootstrap.ts` (`[Hooks Pending]` / `[Hooks Outdated]` / `[Hooks Erroring]`). Example: `skills/compact-on-intent-trap/SKILL.md`.",
                "level": 3,
                "children": [],
                "links": [
