              {
                "target_type": "term",
                "term_name": "preventStop guard",
                "comment": "Natural-language condition on a pinned todo that blocks the end of the turn while it holds; evaluated at STOP in one batched forkChat, fails open."
              },
              {
                "target_type": "term",
                "term_name": "[STOP BLOCKED] note",
                "comment": "SYSTEM note injected on a held guard; STOP returns COLLECT WITHOUT markTurnBoundary() so the turn genuinely continues."
              },
              {
                "target_type": "term",
                "term_name": "TurnVars.preventStopHolds",
                "comment": "Per-todo-id consecutive hold counter that escalates the STOP BLOCKED note from the 2nd hold; lives on TurnVars because a hold never ends the turn."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "/mycc.md/webui-features",
            "text": "A Vue 3-based WebUI is served by mycc itself via an embedded Express + Vite + WebSocket stack (`src/serve/serve-hub.ts`, `src/web/`). It provides a browser-based chat interface as an alternative to the terminal REPL: Markdown rendering (letter-box → chat bubbles); interactive **cards** replacing terminal `ask()` prompts (input/confirm/choice) — `CardItem.vue`; session history via `/history` (backed by the durable triologue JSONL transcript, survives serve stop/restart and page closes); 30s disconnect-reconnect timer with graceful warm shutdown. For the developer reference (component layout, WS protocol, input/card bridges, reconnect replay), see `src/web/README.md`.\n\n**steering (WebUI mid-task direction):** lets the user queue direction for the agent *while the LLM is mid-run* without interrupting it. The buffer is a **lazy process-wide singleton** `getSteeringManager()` (`src/loop/steering-manager.ts`; API `addNote`/`peekNotes`/`peekTexts`/`drainNotes`/`isNonEmpty`/`takeForDelivery`/`resolveBoomerang`/`clear`), distinct from the file-backed **mail** system. `ServeHub` is the **sole writer**: `pushSteer` → `addNote` → `journalUserSubmission(text,'steer')` → `steer-echo` → flush; `resolveSteering` → atomic `resolveBoomerang` split (selected → `submitInput(joinSteeringNotes(...))`; discarded → verbose discarded-ids log) supports per-note discard/send. Loop states are pure **readers**. Three delivery seams re-run the pure check `takeForDelivery(isInputBlocked(), isWrapUpInFlight())` through the shared private `flushSteeringAtSeam()` (`serve-hub.ts`): **WRITE** (`pushSteer`), **ARM** (`waitForInput` armed), **WAKE** (`onWrapUpSettled()` called directly by `esc-wrap-up.ts` on both settle paths, gated on `isRunning()`). **Two consumption paths**: (1) **COLLECT** (`src/loop/states/collect.ts`, step 2c) — in-flight notes drained and injected verbatim as a `REMINDER` (no synthesis); (2) **PROMPT** (`src/loop/states/prompt.ts`) — if the run was interrupted (ESC/停止) and the user submits a fresh query, the held notes are merged into the submission via `peekTexts`/`drainNotes` (`hub` retained only for file uploads + flush broadcast); the two paths are mutually exclusive (PROMPT drains first). Lifecycle (A2): `stop()` calls `manager.clear()` only when `!this.restarting` — held notes **survive `restartServe()`** and are wiped on terminal stop; both `WebInputProvider` fallback branches clear on entry-fallback + post-abort (restart branches return before any wipe). Frontend unchanged (`src/web/src/main.ts`, `ChatInput.vue`, `SteeringBuffer.vue`): when `isRunning`, `send()` routes to `sendSteer`; the buffer bar is populated solely by the server's `steer-echo` broadcast (single source of truth — no local push); `steer-flush` clears it. `/history` returns `{ messages, steeringBuffer }` where `steeringBuffer` = `manager.peekNotes()` (`{id,text}[]`; ETag folds in steering-length + `agentRunning`). Import boundary (A6, enforced by `src/tests/loop/steering-boundary.test.ts`): no `src/loop/**` file may call hub steering methods or import `serve-registry`.\n\n**file upload (WebUI chat-box attachments):** mirrors the steering design — same ephemeral-queue architecture in `ServeHub` (`fileUploadQueue`), same two consumption paths (COLLECT in-flight vs PROMPT stale). Key contrast: file uploads are **informational resources saved and noted, never synthesized** — no `forkChat` merge at PROMPT. Files travel inline in the JSON `WsMessage` as base64 (no multer/multipart); both `input` and `steer` carry an optional `files` array. COLLECT (step 2d) drains and saves to `./.mycc/uploaded/` as `${Date.now()}_${filename}` (base64-decoded), injecting a `REMINDER` listing each file (with truncated user-text preview if provided). PROMPT drains stale files with the same save logic and a `REMINDER` — no synthesis (files are read via `read_picture`/`read_file` in the next turn). No client-side buffer bar for files (`file-upload`/`file-flush` echoes are no-ops). The upload queue is not in `/history` and does not survive a serve stop/restart.\n\n**neglection and esc return:** neglection is triggered when the user presses ESC during LLM inference — signals the agent to quickly wrap up without further tool calls. \"Neglected mode\" aborts ongoing LLM calls, buffers subsequent output, forces a text-only response. Key: `agentIO.isNeglectedMode()`, `setNeglectedMode(value)`, `onNeglected(callback)`; IPC message `{ type: 'neglection' }` (coordinator → lead on ESC).\n\n**esc-aware wrap-up:** on ESC during LLM inference the system enters **wrap-up mode** — the LLM call is aborted via AbortController, a quick \"wrap-up\" LLM call runs in background to produce a concise text-only response, the prompt line reappears immediately, and the wrap-up result is displayed when ready (with commit/rollback logic). Grace period: if the user starts typing before wrap-up completes, the result is discarded. See `docs/loop/esc-wrap-up-redesign.md`. `ctx.core.escAware(operation, onCleanUp)` wraps slow operations for ESC-aware quick return — on ESC the original promise continues in background, `onCleanUp` is invoked immediately, its result returned to the caller. `Core.escAware()` (parent) uses `agentIO.onNeglected()`; `ChildCore.escAware()` is a placeholder (TODO: IPC). Use `escAware` for high-level operations (tool execution, file ops, network requests); use a manual `AbortController` for low-level stream handling (`retryChat()`, hint round). Currently used by tool execution (`src/loop/states/tool.ts`).\n\n**crossroad:** improves LLM response quality by detecting \"turning words\" (e.g., \"However\", \"Wait\", \"但\", \"但是\") in the draft response, generating alternative continuations via parallel `forkChat` calls, selecting the best path while preserving prompt cache. Implementation: `src/hook/crossroad.ts` (runs in the HOOK state before tool execution; debug with `--debug-tp`). Consecutive crossroads contribute to the hint round confusion index.\n\n**@-prefix teammate label convention:** teammate tool output and status messages are routed to a separate `state.teammateMessages` array rather than the main chat log. Routing is decided by a string convention on the existing `label` field — no new WS message types, no `sender` field. The label is `@<teammate>/<tool>` (e.g., `@coder/bash`); `@` marks a teammate message, `/` splits teammate name from tool name. No tool tag → `@<teammate>`. Data flow: the tool tag was historically dropped at the IPC boundary, so **child** (`src/context/child/core.ts`, `ChildCore.brief()`) forwards `tool` in the `log` IPC payload, and **parent** (`src/context/parent/team.ts`, `handleChildMessage()`) builds `@${sender}/${tool}` (falls back to `@${sender}`). Other lifecycle paths (`teammate_ready`, `eta_update`, `status`, `exit`/`error`) are intentionally NOT prefixed. Frontend (`src/web/src/main.ts`): messages whose `label` starts with `@` go into `teammateMessages`; `/history` returns a flat array the client splits. Approximate persistence: teammate messages flow through the same `messageLog` (`MAX_LOG_SIZE = 1000`), replayed on reconnect, but lost on serve stop/restart (the transcript records teammate turns, not their brief/log output).\n\n**Teammate accordion UI:** teammate messages grouped by name and rendered in an accordion UI rather than mixed into the main chat. **`TeammateCard.vue`** — floating top-right card, one row per active teammate (`@name(count): currentTool`), click to open the drawer; hides when the drawer is open or no teammate messages. **`TeammateDrawer.vue`** — right-half panel with stacked accordions per teammate; header `@name(count): current_tool`, body is a flat chronological timeline with `[tool]` prefix tags; first accordion expanded by default; multiple may be open; ✕ closes. Grouping is a frontend computed property — no backend per-teammate state.",
            "title": "WebUI Features",
            "summary": "Verified the WebUI section against source. A Vue 3 SPA is served in-process by `ServeHub` (Express + Vite + `/ws` on one port): Markdown bubbles, interactive cards (`CardItem.vue`) replacing `ask()`, durable `/history` from the triologue JSONL with a revision-derived ETag (folds in `agentRunning`), a 1.5s client reconnect and 30s server disconnect → warm `gracefulShutdown()`. The frontend is now a **`WebuiPhase` FSM** (`idle/submitted/working/prompt/card/await`) in `chat-store.ts`, with `isRunning`/`isWaiting`/`hasPendingCard` as derived getters, and all message handling centralized in the DOM-free `message-dispatch.ts`.\n\n**Corrections for this section:**\n- **Steering protocol changed.** `steer-echo`/`steer-flush` are gone. Every `SteeringManager` mutation bumps a monotonic `revision` and emits a full snapshot via `onChange`; `ServeHub` registers exactly one observer and broadcasts **`steer-state`** (`{steeringRevision, notes}`). The client's `adoptSteering()` accepts only strictly newer revisions, deriving `steeringBuffer = queue − pendingSteeringReview` — so `/history` returns `{messages, steeringBuffer, isRunning}` and stale snapshots can't resurrect resolved notes. Per-note send/discard is now `SteeringReviewCard.vue` at PROMPT; delivery confirmation is structural (surviving ids), so the old resolve guard and steering-length ETag are gone. PROMPT path still synthesizes via `synthesizeWithSteering` (forkChat).\n- **Confirmed:** `takeForDelivery` + three seams (WRITE/ARM/WAKE) in `flushSteeringAtSeam()`; COLLECT step 2c REMINDER and 2d file uploads (base64 in the JSON frame, saved to `./.mycc/uploaded/` as `${Date.now()}_${filename}`, never synthesized; `file-upload`/`file-flush` are client no-ops); neglection (`agentIO.isNeglectedMode/setNeglectedMode/onNeglected`, IPC `{type:'neglection'}`); `escAware` used by tool execution; `@<teammate>/<tool>` labelling built in `team.ts`/`ChildCore.brief()`; `TeammateCard.vue` + `TeammateDrawer.vue` accordions (first expanded, multiple open, ✕ closes).\n- **Crossroad:** lives at `src/loop/crossroad.ts`, invoked from `llm.ts` and resolved in the HOOK stage; it now renders a structured crossroad card (`crossroad-card.ts`). It is disabled by `--disable-crossroad` — **not** debugged by `--debug-tp` (that flag is triologue-parity).\n\nKey terms: `steer-state`, `adoptSteering`, `WebuiPhase FSM`, steering, `takeForDelivery`, neglected mode, crossroad, wrap-up mode.",
            "level": 2,
